<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 9.999 percent from 10.014 percent at the previous auction on January 22.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: May 1, 1997 (April 24, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.999 percent (10.014)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 803.200 million (984.500 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 938.2 million (1.185 billion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.501-10.120 percent (9.501-10.196)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.501-10.200 percent (9.501-10.200)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 111 (147)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 117 (151)</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 Egyptian pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
